docs/phase-1-plan.md:1:# Phase 1 Plan: Investment Copilot (read-only)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:3:Source of truth: `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md` (v9). Screen states from `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md` and the wireframes. This plan covers only PRD §6 Phase 1 as scoped in the kickoff brief. Revision 2 incorporates the counselors PRD review (codex-5.5-high, claude-fable; outputs in `agents/counselors/1788296923-*`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:5:Sections: decisions, migrations, jobs, tool surface, journal builder, stops and open risk, snapshots, UI, testing, deploy, build order, deferred items, Schwab assumptions, working method.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:9:## 0. Decisions (resolved 2026-09-01)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:13:3. **Web login is passwordless magic link**, built on the Rails 8 auth generator with `generates_token_for :magic_link` (15 min, single use). Users are seeded, not self-registered: john@athayde.com and whitney@athayde.com only. No gem. Because a second person can log in, `audit_events.user_id` exists from day one so Phase 2 approvals are attributable. Fallback when email is down: `bin/rails login:link[email]` prints a magic link to the console.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:15:5. **`evaluate_hypothetical_order` omitted** from Phase 1. `get_risk_rules` ships and returns the (empty) `risk_rules` rows.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:16:6. **§5.12 allocation tables deferred** to Phase 2.5.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:17:7. **Off-hours cadence** for orders/transactions sync: hourly.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:22:## 1. Migrations (in creation order)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:24:All money columns `decimal(18,4)`, quantities `decimal(18,6)` (fractional shares unverified, PRD §5.12). All timestamps `timestamptz`. No table stores a bare ticker as a key; instrument references are `instrument_id`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:31:| 4 | `instruments` | `cusip` (nullable, unique where present), `schwab_instrument_id` (nullable, unique where present), `symbol`, `symbol_history` jsonb `[{symbol, seen_at}]`, `asset_type`, `leveraged` bool default false, `description`, `predecessor_instrument_id` (self FK, set on CUSIP succession: reverse split, merger, spin-off). Identity resolution order: CUSIP, then Schwab instrument id, then symbol+asset_type as last resort with a `needs_review` audit. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:32:| 5 | `positions` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `quantity`, `average_price`, `cost_basis`, `market_value`, `last_price`, `working_stop_order_id` (FK orders, nullable), `synced_at`, `raw` jsonb. Unique on (account, instrument). Rows absent from the broker response are deleted on sync. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:34:| 7 | `orders` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `broker_order_id` (unique per account), `status` enum incl. Phase 2 states, `side`, `quantity`, `filled_quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `duration`, `session`, `tax_lot_method`, `placed_via` enum (schwab_direct/app), `parent_order_id` (self FK, bracket child), `replaces_order_id` (self FK, cancel/replace chain), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `entered_at`, `closed_at`, `raw` jsonb | yes (sync only) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:35:| 8 | `order_proposals` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `kind` enum (entry, exit, stop_adjustment), `target_order_id` (nullable, for stop adjustments), `origin` enum (agent/human), `user_id` (nullable), `status` enum (proposed, validated, rejected, approved, submitted, submission_unknown, filled, cancelled), `side`, `quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `target_price`, `thesis`, `setup_id`, `guardrail_results` jsonb, `risk_rule_version`, `acknowledged_warnings` jsonb, `override_reason`, `reject_reason`, `approved_at`, `submitted_at` | no |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:36:| 9 | `submission_attempts` | `order_proposal_id`, `attempted_at`, `payload` jsonb, `response` jsonb, `outcome` enum (submitted, unknown, failed, reconciled), `reconciled_order_id` (nullable) | no |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:37:| 10 | `transactions` | One row per Schwab activity. `account_id`, `instrument_id` (nullable for cash-only), `order_id` (FK, nullable), `broker_order_id` (nullable), `broker_transaction_id` (unique), `kind` enum (fill, dividend, interest, fee, deposit, withdrawal, corporate_action, other), `sub_type` string (raw Schwab type), `side`, `quantity`, `price`, `commission`, `fees` (summed from the activity's fee transfer items), `net_amount`, `trade_date`, `settlement_date`, `executed_at`, `raw` jsonb, `journaled_at` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:39:| 12 | `trades` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `setup_id` (nullable), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `status` enum (open, closed) only, `needs_review` bool (orphan or bootstrapped, missing setup/stop), `bootstrapped` bool (created from an existing position, entry history unavailable), `opened_at` (nullable when bootstrapped), `closed_at`, `avg_entry`, `avg_exit`, `peak_quantity`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target`, `initial_risk`, `realized_pnl`, `realized_r`, `thesis`, `post_mortem`, `followed_setup` (nullable bool), `journal_completed_at` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:40:| 13 | `trade_legs` | `trade_id`, `transaction_id` (unique, nullable for synthetic bootstrap legs), `kind` enum (entry, exit, adjustment, income), `quantity`, `price`, `ratio` (splits), `cash_amount`, `executed_at`, `note` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:41:| 14 | `risk_rules` | `rule_type`, `params` jsonb, `active`, `version`, `setup_id` (nullable), `superseded_by_id` | no |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:42:| 15 | `snapshots` | `account_id`, `as_of` date (unique per account), `equity`, `net_flows` (day), `daily_return` (net of flows), `index_value` (chain-linked, starts at 1.0), `high_water_index`, `drawdown_pct`, `open_risk_amount`, `open_risk_pct`, `unprotected_count`. Fully rebuildable from `balances` + `transactions`. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:43:| 16 | `audit_events` | `kind` string, `actor` enum (human/system/agent), `user_id` (nullable), `subject` polymorphic (nullable), `data` jsonb, `reason`, `created_at` only. Postgres trigger rejects UPDATE/DELETE. Reserved for the PRD's "logged" list; not telemetry. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:45:| 18 | `sync_runs` | `feed` enum (accounts, positions, balances, orders, transactions, market_hours, memory_repo, snapshots), `status` (running, succeeded, failed, skipped_token), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `error`, `records_touched`, `window_from`, `window_to` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:47:| 20 | `tool_calls` | `agent_run_id` (nullable), `transport` enum (mcp, scheduled), `tool_name`, `arguments` jsonb, `duration_ms`, `error`, `created_at`. This is where MCP and runtime tool telemetry goes, not `audit_events`. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:52:Phase 2 columns present now so `orders`/`order_proposals` never need a shape change: `parent_order_id`, `replaces_order_id`, `order_proposal_id`, `submission_unknown` state, `submission_attempts`, `guardrail_results`, `risk_rule_version`, `acknowledged_warnings`, `kind`/`target_order_id` for stop adjustments.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:56:## 2. Jobs (Solid Queue, `config/recurring.yml`, all times America/New_York)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:| `Sync::TickJob` | every 5 min | Sole scheduled sync entry point. Refreshes `market_days` if today or the next 7 days are missing (one call per date). Due checks compare against last *started* time with 1-minute slack. Enqueues: positions+balances (15 min inside the full session window pre-market through post-market, 60 min otherwise); orders+transactions (5 min inside the session, 60 min otherwise); `Snapshots::DailyJob` once per market day after `regular_closes_at` + 20 min and after a successful positions sync since close. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:66:| `Sync::PositionsJob` | via tick | `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions`; resolve instruments, upsert positions, delete positions absent from the response, append a `balances` row; then `Journal::BootstrapJob` for trading-enabled accounts |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:67:| `Sync::OrdersJob` | via tick | Window: `fromEnteredTime` = max(last success − 1 day, now − 60 days); plus a daily pull with `status=WORKING` so GTC orders older than the window stay tracked (both unverified). Upsert; walk `replaces_order_id` chains; set `placed_via: schwab_direct` when no proposal matches; update `positions.working_stop_order_id` (see §5) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:69:| `Sync::CatchUpJob` | after re-auth | Accounts, positions, orders, transactions with widened windows |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:70:| `Journal::BootstrapJob` | after positions sync | See §4 |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:71:| `Journal::LinkFillsJob` | after transactions sync | See §4 |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:73:| `Snapshots::DailyJob` | via tick | See §6 |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:76:| `Agent::MorningBriefJob` | 07:00 market days | See §3 |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:77:| `Agent::EndOfDayJob` | 16:30 market days | See §3 |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:84:## 3. Tool surface (one registry, two transports)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:90:| `get_portfolio` | Positions with last price, unrealized P&L, working stop, distance to stop, per-position open risk, `unprotected` flag, synced_at per row |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:94:| `get_journal(filters)` | Trades with legs; filters: status, needs_review, setup, instrument, date range, missing_post_mortem |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:96:| `get_risk_rules` | Active `risk_rules` rows (empty in Phase 1) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:98:Every call writes a `tool_calls` row. Nothing in this section writes to `audit_events`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:106:## 4. Journal builder (zero-to-zero, trading-enabled accounts only)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:108:IRA and other read-only accounts sync positions and transactions (for Phase 2 wash-sale checks) but never create trades.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:110:**Bootstrap** (`Journal::BootstrapJob`, after every positions sync): for each position in a trading-enabled account with no open trade, create a trade with `bootstrapped: true, needs_review: true, status: open`, `avg_entry` = broker average price, `peak_quantity` = quantity, `opened_at` nil, one synthetic `entry` leg with no transaction. This covers day-one holdings and any position whose entry fills are beyond the 60-day transactions window.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:112:**Link fills** (`Journal::LinkFillsJob`), per account and instrument, transactions in `executed_at` order, skipping already-journaled rows:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:113:- Buy fill, no open trade: open a trade. If `transactions.order_id` → `orders.order_proposal_id` resolves, copy setup, thesis, planned stop, target; else `needs_review: true`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:117:- `initial_risk` = quantity of the first entry leg × (its price − `planned_stop`), fixed at that moment. `realized_r` = `realized_pnl` / `initial_risk`, nil when no planned stop.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:119:- Split or reverse split: `adjustment` leg with `ratio`, zero cash; `quantity`, `avg_entry`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target` scaled by the ratio.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:121:- CUSIP succession (merger, spin-off, reverse split issuing a new CUSIP): when an `out` on instrument A and an `in` on instrument B arrive as one corporate-action activity or within the same activity group, set `instruments.predecessor_instrument_id` on B and move the open trade to B with an `adjustment` leg. Unmatched halves fall back to normal exit/entry handling with `needs_review`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:122:- Symbol change on a known CUSIP: update `instruments.symbol`, append `symbol_history`, trades untouched.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:123:- Idempotent via the unique index on `trade_legs.transaction_id`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:125:**Review path** (Flow 4 plus the Monarch-style orphan review from the flows doc): trades with `needs_review` show a "N trades need review" banner on the dashboard. The review form takes setup, planned stop, and thesis; saving clears `needs_review`, computes `initial_risk`, and audits `trade_reviewed`. The post-mortem form (one line plus followed/improvised) is separate and available on any closed trade.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:129:## 5. Stops and open risk in Phase 1
docs/phase-1-plan.md:131:No stop is not zero risk. `Sync::OrdersJob` identifies, per position, a working broker-side stop: a sell order on the same instrument with `order_type` STOP or STOP_LIMIT and status in the working set (WORKING, ACCEPTED, QUEUED, PENDING_ACTIVATION; enum unverified), following `replaces_order_id` chains. It sets `positions.working_stop_order_id` or clears it.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:133:- Protected position: distance to stop = (last − stop) / last; open risk = quantity × (last − stop).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:134:- Unprotected position: `unprotected` flag, distance and risk shown as unknown, never zero.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:135:- Portfolio open risk = sum over protected positions, and the dashboard and `get_account_health` state how many positions are excluded as unprotected.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:139:## 6. Snapshots (per account, chain-linked)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:146:- `open_risk_amount`, `open_risk_pct`, `unprotected_count` from §5 at snapshot time.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:151:## 7. UI (Hotwire, mobile-responsive, no JS routers, no hover-dependent modals)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:155:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner (healthy / expiring / expired / halted), equity + day change, open risk with unprotected count, settled/unsettled cash, positions list with distance-to-stop as the primary number and inline `unprotected` where applicable, "N trades need review" callout, pending proposals count (0), staleness stamps on every number, empty state before first sync |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:156:| Trade review | `/trades/:id/review` | Setup, planned stop, thesis for `needs_review` trades; "N more to review" progression |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:157:| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List and detail; Flow 4 quick entry (one line + followed/improvised) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:168:## 8. Testing
docs/phase-1-plan.md:170:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:178:## 9. Deploy
docs/phase-1-plan.md:182:- `bin/dokku-setup`: documents postgres plugin, letsencrypt, config vars (`RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, `MEMORY_REPO_PATH`), storage mount for the memory repo, `ps:scale worker=1`, and the daily offsite DB dump from PRD §5.9 (postgres plugin backup to object storage on a cron).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:187:## 10. Build order (green `bin/ci` at each step)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:191:3. Schwab adapter: `Schwab::Client` (OAuth, accounts, positions, orders, transactions, market hours, quotes, price history) with retry/backoff/limiter, `Schwab::FakeClient`, response mappers, `docs/verify-on-approval.md` started from §12.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:193:5. Sync jobs, market calendar, tick scheduler, `sync_runs`, working-stop detection.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:194:6. Journal builder (bootstrap, link, review path) + setup stats + snapshots.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:202:## 11. Explicitly not built in Phase 1
docs/phase-1-plan.md:204:Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:208:## 12. Schwab assumptions to verify on approval (seed for `docs/verify-on-approval.md`)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:210:From PRD §9: exact `TaxLotMethod` enum values; order-endpoint rate limits. Added by this plan:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:211:- `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions` returns balances in the same payload (`currentBalances`, `initialBalances`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:217:- Order status enum values for "working" stops; cancel/replace produces a new order id and marks the old one REPLACED.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:218:- Fractional-share quantities in positions and orders.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:224:## 13. Working method, per phase and per build step
docs/phase-1-plan.md:226:Each numbered step in §10 that ships a feature runs this loop:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:229:2. **Build** the feature vertically per §10.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:230:3. **RSpec green** and reviewed for coverage against the §8 priority list, not just passing.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:1:# PRD: Investment Copilot (working title)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:7:## 1. Summary
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:13:## 2. Goals
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:15:- Positions, balances, orders, and transactions synced from Schwab automatically. No hand-maintained portfolio.csv.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:16:- A trade journal with per-setup expectancy stats that is populated from actual fills, not memory.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:17:- A guardrail engine (risk rules as data, not vibes) that evaluates every proposed order before it can reach Schwab.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:21:## 3. Non-Goals (v1)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:29:## 4. Architecture
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:53:## 5. Components
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:55:### 5.1 Schwab Integration (Rails)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:65:- **Order submission idempotency:** the Schwab order POST has no client-supplied order id (per community clients; confirm post-approval), so dedupe is local. The approved → submitted transition runs under a row lock and is the only code path that can call the order endpoint. On an ambiguous outcome (timeout, 5xx, connection drop after send), the proposal enters `submission_unknown`; a reconciliation job queries the orders endpoint for a matching order (instrument, qty, side, price, time window) before any retry. No blind retries, ever.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:67:### 5.2 Data Model (core tables)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:70:- `instruments` (CUSIP as the stable key; current symbol, symbol history, asset type, leveraged flag). Every other table references instrument_id, never a raw ticker, so ticker changes cannot break linking.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:71:- `positions` (account, instrument, qty, cost basis, synced_at): always broker-derived
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:72:- `orders` (broker order id, status, side, instrument, qty, type, limit/stop, placed_via, parent_order_id for bracket children; see 5.4.2)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:73:- `order_proposals` (agent- or human-initiated; status: proposed → validated/rejected → approved → submitted → filled/cancelled; stores guardrail evaluation results as JSON; carries a submission_attempt record for the ambiguous-outcome path in 5.1)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:75:- `trades` (journal). A trade is one instrument's position lifecycle from zero back to zero; scale-ins and scale-outs are `trade_legs` linked to transactions. Fields: setup tag, thesis, planned stop/target, realized R-multiple, post_mortem. Fills with no originating proposal (orders placed at Schwab directly) create a trade in `incomplete` state with no planned stop; the EOD brief asks for the missing stop/setup rather than computing a bogus R.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:77:- `risk_rules` (rule type, params, active, version): see 5.4
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:78:- `snapshots` (daily equity, open risk $, open risk %, drawdown from HWM). Equity series is flow-adjusted: deposits/withdrawals (from transactions) are excluded from HWM/drawdown math so a deposit never resets a drawdown and a withdrawal never fakes one.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:79:- `audit_events` (append-only: approvals, rejections, collar overrides with reason, rule edits with before/after, kill-switch toggles, re-auths, shadow-mode toggles). Every mention of "logged" elsewhere in this doc means a row here.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:81:### 5.3 Sync Jobs
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:84:- Orders + transactions: every 5 min during market hours (drives journal auto-population).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:85:- Corporate actions/dividends: from transactions feed; adjust journal cost basis automatically.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:89:### 5.4 Guardrail Engine
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:93:1. Max risk per trade: X% of equity (size derived from entry-stop distance).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:94:2. Max concurrent positions; max single-position and single-sector exposure.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:102:8. **Stop collar (see 5.4.1):** every entry proposal must include a stop, and the stop must fall within the computed collar or the proposal is flagged for override.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:108:Purpose: replace gut-feel stop placement with a computed acceptable range ("collar") derived from several standard methods, evaluated against price history from Schwab Market Data (FMP fallback).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:110:Candidate methods (each produces a stop price for a proposed long entry):
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:113:- **Swing structure:** most recent N-bar swing low minus a small buffer (e.g., 0.1-0.3 × ATR). The "invalidated thesis" stop.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:114:- **Percent stop:** entry − p%, p configurable (classic 7-8% max-loss discipline). The hard ceiling on distance.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:120:- Collar = [tightest candidate, widest candidate], with the percent stop acting as an absolute floor (a stop wider than the percent method is never inside the collar).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:121:- Proposal evaluation returns each method's value, the collar bounds, where the proposed stop sits, and the resulting position size under the max-risk-per-trade rule for the chosen stop.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:122:- A stop outside the collar does not hard-block; it requires an explicit human override with a logged reason. (Guardrails 1-7 remain hard blocks where marked.)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:126:- Nightly job recomputes Chandelier/ATR trails for open positions. Where the recomputed trail is tighter than the working stop, the EOD brief surfaces a "tighten stop" suggestion with the numbers. Adjusting the actual stop order remains a human-approved action (Phase 3 candidate for auto-submit of tighten-only adjustments).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:128:Configuration lives in `risk_rules` (method on/off, k, p, N per setup). Method parameters are data, not code, so they can be tuned as the journal accumulates evidence about which stop style fits each setup.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:130:#### 5.4.2 Stop Order Placement (decided: real stops at Schwab)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:132:An app-only stop with 5-15 minute polling is not protection. Every approved entry is submitted as a bracket: the entry order with a one-triggers-another child stop order (Schwab order strategies support this; confirm exact strategy type names post-approval). Consequences:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:134:- `orders` carries `parent_order_id`; the child stop is tracked, synced, and shown on the dashboard as the working stop.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:135:- "Tighten stop" is a cancel/replace of the child order, which goes through the proposal pipeline as a stop-adjustment proposal (guardrails: new stop must be tighter than current for the Phase 3 auto-submit class; any loosening is human-only with a logged reason).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:136:- If the bracket child fails to place after the parent fills, the position is flagged `unprotected` on the dashboard and in a push/email immediately; this is a hard alert, not a brief item.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:137:- Working stops are reconciled against Schwab on every orders sync; a stop that disappears at the broker (cancelled out-of-band) flags the position `unprotected`.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:139:### 5.5 MCP Tool Surface (agent-facing)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:142:- `get_portfolio` (positions with live marks, distance to stop, open risk)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:145:- `get_journal(filters)`, `get_setup_stats`
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:146:- `get_risk_rules`, `evaluate_hypothetical_order(params)` (dry-run guardrails)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:153:Explicitly absent from MCP: submit_order, cancel_order, edit_risk_rules, token operations. Submission happens only in the Rails approval UI (or a signed confirmation link), by the human.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:155:### 5.5a Agent Runtime (where Claude actually runs)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:166:### 5.6 Memory Layer (git repo, read by agent)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:171:- Removed from files because Rails owns them now: portfolio.csv, trades.csv, risk.md (risk rules live in the DB and are surfaced read-only to the agent).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:174:### 5.7 Scheduled Workflows (agent, via Rails-triggered runs)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:176:- 07:00 ET pre-market brief: overnight moves on holdings/watchlist, gaps, today's earnings/econ events touching the book, stops at risk, settled-cash status. Delivered by email.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:177:- 16:30 ET end-of-day: fills recap, journal rows created, missing post-mortems flagged, equity snapshot.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:181:### 5.8 UI (Rails, Hotwire)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:183:Mobile is in scope: everything renders on a phone; proposal detail, dashboard glance, and journal quick-entry are mobile-first. Full screen inventory, flows, and per-screen states live in the companion doc `investment-copilot-ui-flows.md`; John designs against that. Summary:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:188:- Trade detail / 30-second journal entry
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:193:### 5.8a iOS App (decided: native, private, iOS only)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:196:- **What the native shell adds:** APNs push, Face ID / device passcode as the deliberate confirm on Approve (resolves the open question in the flows doc: the second gesture is biometric, not a slide), app icon and home-screen presence, native navigation stack. Path configuration marks proposal detail, dashboard, and journal entry as the mobile-first routes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:202:### 5.9 Deployment (decided)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:211:### 5.10 Weekly Ritual (decided: Sundays, email)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:218:### 5.11 Testing & CI (mirrors Talos / Patchvault conventions)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:221:  1. Guardrail engine: exhaustive unit specs per rule, including the interaction cases (CSP-style cash reservation vs GFV check is Phase 3, but settled-cash math, wash-sale window, and stop-collar bounds are Phase 1-2). Table-driven specs so each rule's edge cases are enumerable.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:225:  5. Sync jobs: fixture payloads for positions/transactions, including corporate-action and dividend events, verifying journal linking.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:226:- **Playwright** for clickable UI: approval queue flow (approve/reject a proposal, override a stop outside the collar with a logged reason), dashboard renders with seeded data, risk-rule editor. These run against a seeded test DB with a fake Schwab adapter, not cassettes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:230:### 5.12 Allocation Module (cycle-pattern mechanics)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:232:A second rule set alongside the trading guardrails, covering the book-level behaviors from post-crash market research (concentration of best days, lump-sum vs staged deployment, threshold rebalancing, correlation breakdown, leveraged-proxy discipline). Kept structurally separate from per-trade guardrails: trading rules judge one order, allocation rules judge the whole book. Both feed the same proposal → approval pipeline; nothing here auto-executes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:234:**Data model additions:** `allocation_targets` (asset or class, target weight, drift band), `instrument_tags` (leveraged/amplified flag per symbol), `deployment_policies` (per cash-inflow handling).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:238:1. **Threshold rebalancing.** Nightly drift check against `allocation_targets`. When any weight drifts beyond its band (default 5 percentage points, per-target configurable), the agent generates rebalance proposals (sell overweight, buy underweight) through the normal pipeline with guardrail evaluation. The rule is mechanical; the approval is still human. A minimum trade notional (configurable, e.g., $100) suppresses churn on a small account; drift that would require a sub-minimum order is reported, not proposed. Fractional-share support in the order API is unverified; until confirmed, quantities round down to whole shares.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:239:2. **Leveraged-proxy exception.** Symbols tagged leveraged/amplified are excluded from mechanical rebalance proposals. Drift on those instead triggers a thesis-review task: the proposal renders the original thesis from the journal/watchlist next to current numbers, and the human decides deploy / hold / exit. Encodes "the discipline is the same, the decision is not mechanical."
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:242:5. **Correlation stress check.** Weekly job computes rolling 60-day correlations between each holding (and tagged "diversifier" instruments) and SPY from price history. When a diversifier's correlation exceeds a threshold (default 0.6), the Sunday review flags that the diversification assumption is currently failing. Diagnostic only.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:247:**UI:** allocation targets + drift live on the dashboard below positions; rebalance and deployment proposals use the standard Flow-2 proposal detail; thesis-review proposals add the original-thesis panel. Rule authoring goes in the (desktop) rule editor.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:249:## 6. Phasing
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:251:**Phase 1 (read-only):** Schwab OAuth + token lifecycle, account/position/transaction sync, dashboard, journal auto-population from fills, memory repo, MCP read tools, daily briefs.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:252:**Phase 2 (propose + approve):** guardrail engine, order proposals via MCP, approval UI, bracket submission (entry + child stop, 5.4.2) from UI, ambiguous-outcome reconciliation, settlement checks from broker balances, wash-sale checks against the linked IRA, Hotwire Native iOS app with push and Face ID confirm (5.8a). Ships with shadow mode on.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:253:**Phase 2.5 (allocation module):** targets, drift checks, rebalance/deployment proposals, correlation and cash-drag diagnostics in the Sunday review (§5.12).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:254:**Phase 3 (earned automation):** conditional auto-submit for a narrow class (e.g., pre-approved stop adjustments) only after the journal shows positive expectancy over a real sample; kill-switch; per-day order caps.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:256:## 7. Decisions Log
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:263:- Agent never submits orders; proposal/approval split confirmed.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:269:- Review v8 (Sep 1): real bracket stops at Schwab; local idempotency with reconcile-before-retry; unattended runtime is read-only; trades defined as zero-to-zero lifecycles keyed by CUSIP; shadow mode on by default; broker balances as settled-cash source; market calendar from Schwab; flow-adjusted equity series; min rebalance notional; single-writer memory repo; one append-only audit table.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:271:## 8. Options Scope (expanded from open question 2)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:275:**Data (resolved):** Schwab Market Data API provides option chains with greeks (delta, gamma, theta, vega, rho), implied volatility, theoretical value, and time value per contract. No local computation needed. Option symbols use OSI format (e.g., `AAPL  250117C00150000`), which touches the symbol handling everywhere: positions sync, journal linking, quotes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:282:**Journal complexity:** R-multiple math changes (risk is premium paid for long options; assignment risk for short options). Expiration and assignment arrive as transaction events that must be linked back to the originating trade, and assignment of a CSP creates a new stock position mid-trade. This is the largest chunk of real work.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:284:**Stop collar:** ATR/swing methods don't map to options premiums. Long options would use a premium-based max-loss rule (e.g., full premium is the risk, sized accordingly) instead of the collar.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:286:**Recommendation:** equities-only through Phase 2. Add a Phase 3 "options module" limited to long options and covered calls first (no CSP collateral logic yet), then CSPs. Rationale: assignment/expiration lifecycle handling and collateral reservation are each roughly the size of the whole equity journal feature, and a tiny cash account gets limited benefit from CSPs anyway (collateral lockup is large relative to account size).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:290:## 9. Open Questions (remaining)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:294:## 10. Risks
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:296:- **7-day refresh token** is the top operational risk; a missed re-auth silently kills all automation. Mitigated by health checks and nags, but it cannot be engineered away.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:298:- Order idempotency: no client order id on the Schwab side, so dedupe is local (row-locked single submission path, `submission_unknown` state, reconcile-before-retry; see 5.1). Duplicate submission is the one bug this system cannot afford.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:299:- Agent hallucination and prompt injection are contained by design: the agent never computes position size or submits orders, and unattended runs cannot create proposals at all (5.5a).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:300:- Unprotected positions: bracket child failing to place or being cancelled out-of-band. Mitigated by immediate hard alert and per-sync reconciliation (5.4.2).

